# Authentication Rules

- Use the authentication mechanism selected by the Laravel technical documentation; do not replace it ad hoc.
- Passwords MUST be hashed with the framework-supported secure password hashing mechanism.
- Tokens/sessions MUST have revocation/expiration behavior documented and tested.
- Recovery flows MUST not disclose whether an account exists beyond the designed UX.
- Login attempts MUST be protected by rate limiting and abuse controls.
- Never log passwords, access tokens, refresh tokens, OTP secrets, or payment secrets.
- Treat phone/email verification as an authentication concern separate from authorization.
- Administrative accounts should support stronger authentication requirements when specified.
